WEBVTT

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:18.530
Wait!

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.680
Mr. Bus Driver!

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.990
Stop!

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.400
Yes!

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:28.900
Thank you!

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.440
What are you, a thug?

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.730
Mr. Bus Driver!

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.740
You little punk, get your ass over here!

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.040
Let's wear proper attire.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.710
Let's wear proper attire.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.590
Let's wear...

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.580
Louder!

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.110
Let's wear proper attire!

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.190
Why you...

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.590
Get it right!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.340
Let's wear proper attire!

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.920
You over there!

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.340
Come here.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.130
What the hell happened to your hair?

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:44.430
Are you trying to rebel or something?

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:45.430
Hey.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:48.930
It's Gargamel.

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:51.810
Come on, just follow me.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.940
What's this now?

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.680
This isn't a shoe, it's a freakin' weapon!

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.760
Are you trying to kill someone?

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:58.860
Go change into new shoes now!

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.360
Hurry up.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.120
I'll pull you up from on top, so bend over.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:14.080
I'll scratch your back if you scratch mine.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.630
Come on.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.380
Don't you dare try to peek, okay?

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.220
How can I even peek when you're so heavy?

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.310
Here, I'll pull you up.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:41.570
Come on.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.580
I'll scratch your back if you scratch mine, right?

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:58.580
I'll pass.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:00.630
Oh?

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:02.460
I'm going then.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.100
Hey, Joonsang?

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:43.880
Come on.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:52.370
You know we're supposed to broadcast together during lunch today, right?

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:54.930
You better show up on time.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.090
What's wrong, Yujin?

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.630
Did something happen yesterday?

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.970
Nothing at all.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.680
I'm telling you, I'm fine.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.640
Are you hurt? Let me see that.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.400
Didn't your mother teach you to respect women?

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:41.770
Hey, Joonsang!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:43.970
What's with the bandage on your face?

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.400
Are you hurt anywhere else?

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.570
Are you all right, Joonsang?

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.410
You should have taken better care of yourself.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.910
What's wrong with <i>you,</i> Yujin?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:01.540
Did you...

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.380
with Joonsang?

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.420
Why aren't you saying anything?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.240
The bell rang already.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.760
Go back to your seat.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:12.720
We'll finish this later.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.940
Why isn't he coming?

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.540
I was actually supposed to go on air with a friend today.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.710
But since he didn't keep his word,

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.600
it looks like I'll have to broadcast by myself the entire time,

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.760
without being able to eat lunch.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:52.510
I'm not going to name any names,

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.220
but if you are listening to this right now,

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.760
I hope you think about what you've done.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.600
I shouldn't talk about my own personal feelings on air, you say?

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.290
Please forgive me just this once.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.350
Here's our first song of the day;

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:07.130
it's an upbeat song

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.550
that most accurately describes my feelings right now:

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:10.480
"Oh My God."

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:29.030
Anyone got more rice?

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.050
You still want more?

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:31.010
Here, take mine.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.610
I said don't look at that!

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:39.370
Hey!

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:41.830
Stop that!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:43.770
What was that?

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.370
What was that just now?

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:47.670
My heart just skipped a beat.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:48.540
That was Yujin.

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:50.040
Hold this for a sec.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:51.670
Hey, Yongguk!

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.300
Wait up!

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:58.680
Yujin.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:09:59.390
Yujin!

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:00.800
What's wrong?

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:01.850
I don't know.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:07.730
Hey, where are you going?

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:10.100
Joonsang,

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.250
what happened?

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.570
What's wrong with Yujin?

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:15.650
Are you worrying about her or are you blaming me?

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:16.740
What?

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.070
Why don't you just pick one.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.280
Let's go!

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.040
Let's do this!

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.080
Let's go, Joonsang!

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.120
Here it comes!

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:31.290
I got it, rebound!

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:32.460
My ball!

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:36.460
Nice spike!

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:39.590
Go, Joonsang!

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.390
You're so cool!

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.690
Good job!

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.400
Nice, let's keep it up!

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:56.030
One more!

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.570
Get this one!

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.360
Don't mess up!

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.040
Sanghyuk!

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:09.910
Are you all right?

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:13.630
Keep playing!

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:14.630
Time out.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.630
What is it?

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:18.960
You guys, get together.

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:22.510
Don't you think you're going a little overboard, Joonsang?

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:23.390
What?

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.040
Think about teamwork, man;

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.100
you can't handle every attack.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.890
What's your problem, we're winning.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:32.940
Don't you know that winning isn't everything?

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:34.630
Where does it say that?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.480
Do your <i>textbooks</i> say that winning doesn't matter?

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.950
Damn teacher's pet.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:42.950
What did you just say?

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.120
Hit me.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:48.690
What's wrong?

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.750
Did your books tell you not to hit people as well?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.210
Fucking teacher's pet.

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:15.270
Do you have something against Sanghyuk?

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:21.650
You don't look like you like him very much.

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:23.260
I'm not saying this just because he's my friend:

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.910
he's a really nice guy.

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:25.530
So what?

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:26.910
So...

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:35.370
I'm just saying you're overreacting a little.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.250
Are you two going out?

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:40.380
What?

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.190
It's nothing like that!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:47.050
We've just been friends since we were little, and—

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.270
I can do it fine with the right hand.

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:01.440
I can do it fine with the left hand.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.410
So why can't I do it with both hands together?

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:13.470
You're my only hope, Yongguk.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:15.500
How many points do you think I'll get?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:17.960
Let's see.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.460
Let's see now, how many points will you get?

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.010
Will it be 100 out of 100 or 0...

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:26.430
This is making my palms sweaty.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:28.220
Let's see.

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:31.980
Five points.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:32.930
Yup, five.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:36.100
Really? What should I do?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.690
Just accept it as your fate and move on.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.070
Really?

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.670
But I practiced so hard...

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:46.280
Mommy...

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:47.980
Don't worry.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:50.660
I'm sure she'll give you an "A" for effort.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.280
Yeah right...

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.960
Hey, Yongguk, can you take just one more look at it?

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.580
Who knows, maybe we'll get a different result this time...

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:00.710
Please?

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:04.460
Hey, Joonsang,

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.380
come with me for a bit.

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:12.050
Sit here.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:17.560
Keep your hands round as if you're holding eggs inside them.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:18.230
Why?

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:19.730
Can't you tell?

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:21.610
I'm trying to teach you piano.

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:25.990
I bet you didn't know we have a piano exam today.

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:31.490
I'm the type that always has to pay favors back.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.490
Keep your wrists up.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.910
This is hopeless; watch me play first.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:40.750
Come on, watch.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.240
I forget the rest.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:20.120
I thought you said you couldn't play piano?

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:22.790
I never said that.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.220
What's this song called?

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:15.300
Don't you know it too?

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.100
I thought I heard you humming along.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:22.040
I remember the melody,

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.520
but I don't remember what it's called

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:26.060
or where I heard it.

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:28.650
"The First Time".

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.450
The song's called, "The First Time".

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:36.030
"The First Time"?

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:11.320
You didn't move here from Seoul because you raised hell in school, did you?

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:13.070
Who said that?

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:15.900
You didn't, right?

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:20.160
You couldn't have, since you really suck at fighting.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.910
So, why did you move here?

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:30.920
I guess we're not good enough friends for you to tell me that yet, huh?

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:34.920
Do you want to try paying back that favor in a different way?

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:05.000
Aren't you getting on?

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:14.480
Hey Yujin,

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:18.030
have you heard the story about the Land of Shadows?

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:22.280
A man went to the Land of Shadows,

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:25.740
but no one would talk to him because they were all shadows.

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:28.750
What happened next?

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:32.620
So he was there all lonely by himself.

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:36.090
And that's the end of it.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:40.840
What?

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:42.220
Oh, nothing.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.340
What?

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:47.180
I just found it funny.

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:49.890
"That's the end of it."

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.850
That was just like you, wasn't it?

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:55.190
Why are you so serious?

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:59.190
You always have your guard up and you never smile.

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.320
You're always by yourself.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:13.710
I think you need some friends.

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:19.550
You've got nothing to lose by being friends with the other guys, right?

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.050
I don't need them.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:26.090
Are you sure it's not because you just don't know how to make friends?

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:30.890
It's really easy;

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:33.600
you just have to approach them step by step.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:36.810
You can't just approach one person though.

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:38.440
Look, it's like this.

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:41.300
Left foot, right foot,

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:43.900
right foot,

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:45.820
left foot, right foot...

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:49.740
And as these little steps pile up, you become friends.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.000
Take my hand.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.330
I'm just practicing what you taught me.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:00.630
Step by step, right?

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.150
Oh yeah,

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:28.620
did you find the person you were looking for?

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:30.990
Who was it?

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:32.660
My father.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:34.710
So he didn't die then?

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:39.630
How was it meeting him?

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:44.170
I didn't feel anything at first.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.430
I just wanted to find out what kind of person he is

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.350
and how we're alike.

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:52.890
And then?

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:55.980
He didn't seem to remember me at all.

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:01.900
I wish he'd remember me.

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:07.860
Maybe I hate that person.

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:11.740
He's not just "that person"; he's your father.

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:13.700
It's all right to hate him,

00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:16.290
but don't call him "that person."

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:20.000
And don't lie saying that he's dead either.

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:23.260
You can fool others,

00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:25.340
but you should never fool yourself.

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:31.800
You came here because you wanted to find and meet your father, right?

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:36.430
No matter how much you hate and blame him,

00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:39.230
it's a good thing to have a father.

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:41.480
If he's alive, that is.

00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:49.490
It's getting cold; let's head back.

00:22:49.570 --> 00:22:50.280
Sure.

00:22:52.660 --> 00:22:54.560
Now that's pretty.

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:55.740
Good, now smile.

00:22:56.790 --> 00:22:58.210
I better look good in these pictures, okay?

00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:02.290
Wanna take a picture too?

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:03.960
We don't have a camera, do we?

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:06.760
Should I ask them to take one of us?

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:10.720
Don't move, now.

00:23:10.840 --> 00:23:12.340
Okay, here we go.

00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:14.300
Look over here.

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:17.720
You look awkward; try smiling a bit more.

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:18.990
A little more.

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:19.850
More.

00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:21.310
Okay.

00:23:24.110 --> 00:23:26.320
1 2 3 click!

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:39.290
Sanghyuk...
